{
  "description": "BTPS 1.2 sync. A device's sync is an artifact.send to the user's own address whose transporter envelope names the send it copies: `syncOf: { id, sha256 }`, the sent artifact's id and the lowercase hex SHA-256 of its RFC 8785 form, signature included. `syncOf` is only on an artifact from and to the same address (compared without case), and only in a `1.2.0` artifact. `hash` is a sent artifact and the `syncOf` that names it. A provider refuses a sync sent to it directly (`BTP_ERROR_SYNC_NOT_ALLOWED`): it comes only inside its own device's artifact.send. `delivery` cases are sentbox result entries whose `meta.delivery` is the provider's own record of a send: `status` pending, delivered or failed, an optional BTPS error `code`, and `at`, always.",
